@{
    // Element 7: what a plan change actually means for the publisher.
    //
    // Deliberately does NOT state proration or refund mechanics. Those are Microsoft's billing
    // behaviour and are not documented in the fulfillment reference, so asserting them in a
    // teaching sample would be inventing detail. Everything below is from the lifecycle and
    // operations references linked at the foot.
}
<details class="explainer">
    <summary>@L["What a plan change actually means for you"]</summary>
    <div class="body">
        <div class="pc-figure" role="img" aria-label="@L["One subscription before the change, one subscription after it — only the plan differs."]">
            <div class="pc-box">
                <span class="pc-cap">@L["Before"]</span>
                <code>sub-0001</code>
                <span class="badge subscribed">Subscribed</span>
                <span class="pc-plan">plan: <code>silver</code></span>
            </div>
            <div class="pc-arrow">
                <span class="pc-arrow-line" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
                <span class="pc-arrow-lbl">@L["ChangePlan webhook"]</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pc-box">
                <span class="pc-cap">@L["After"]</span>
                <code>sub-0001</code>
                <span class="badge subscribed">Subscribed</span>
                <span class="pc-plan">plan: <code>gold</code></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="pc-points">
            <li>@L["Still one subscription. The id does not change and no second subscription is created — a plan change is an update, not a new purchase."]</li>
            <li>@L["Only an active subscription can be updated; it stays active throughout."]</li>
            <li>@L["Your job is two things: switch the features to match the new plan, and reply to the Operations API within 10 seconds. No reply within 10 seconds and Microsoft records it as a success anyway."]</li>
            <li>@L["Pricing, proration and invoicing for the change are handled on Microsoft's side. This app never calculates money."]</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="foot">
            @L["Try it: trigger ChangePlan in the emulator and watch the plan, the provenance and the illustrative allowance below all move together."]
            <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/marketplace-offers/pc-saas-fulfillment-life-cycle" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@L["Lifecycle reference"]</a>,
            <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/marketplace-offers/pc-saas-fulfillment-operations-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@L["Operations API reference"]</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</details>
